                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "\"Space Invaders with a twist\" is not an inherently bad idea as there are plenty of games out there which use this formula and manage to come across as a competently designed and fun to play game. 1979 Invasion Earth is not one of those games.\n\nThe game has a lot of things going for it such as decent music and some nice visuals, but when it comes down to things it's just too hard to play this game. The game itself isn't too difficult, it's just too bright, too colorful, and too flashy to see what the hell is going on at any given time. Sprites are very large, move fast, powerups are ridiculously huge, and everything has gigantic particle bloom explosions and/or flavor text that appears when you shoot it. All of these things serve to obscure the screen to the point where the game becomes unplayable due to enemy bullets hiding behind all of the flashiness. If this was an intended game mechanic, then the developers are crazy.\n\nWith a more conservative approach to the game's visuals this really could've been something. Instead it's just a nuclear mess.",
